From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x: fix the HPH and ADC volume dB scales

line_gain was declared DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, 0, 7, 1): 0 dB at
the bottom in 0.07 dB steps, so "HPHL/HPHR Volume" advertised 1.4 dB over
its 21 steps. The headphone PA gain is -30 dB to 0 dB in 1.5 dB steps, as
wcd938x declares for the same block (20 steps x 1.5 dB = the 30 dB range
here). A volume control that claims 1.4 dB makes userspace (PipeWire)
leave it parked and attenuate in software, then the real 30 dB analog
range lands abruptly at the top of the slider: very loud, then clipping.

analog_gain ("ADC1..4 Volume") has the same mistake, 0.25 dB steps; the
ADC gain is 0..30 dB over 20 steps, as wcd938x declares it.

Measured on the KONKR Pocket FIT: stepping HPHL/HPHR Volume 0 -> 10 -> 20
with PipeWire's volume fixed changes the loudness audibly at each step.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
index 8dbd47fca..533998063 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -216,8 +216,8 @@ static const char * const wcd939x_supplies[] = {
 };
 
 static const SNDRV_CTL_TLVD_DECLARE_DB_MINMAX(ear_pa_gain, 600, -1800);
-static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, 0, 7, 1);
-static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(analog_gain, 0, 25, 1);
+static const DECLARE_TLV_DB_SCALE(line_gain, -3000, 150, 0);
+static const SNDRV_CTL_TLVD_DECLARE_DB_MINMAX(analog_gain, 0, 3000);
 
 static const struct wcd_mbhc_field wcd_mbhc_fields[WCD_MBHC_REG_FUNC_MAX] = {
 	WCD_MBHC_FIELD(WCD_MBHC_L_DET_EN, WCD939X_ANA_MBHC_MECH, 0x80),
